google/electra-large-discriminator,59769,pretraining,downloads:desc,2024-02-29T10:20:21.000Z,2022-03-02T23:29:05.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,11,,"**ELECTRA** is a new method for self-supervised language representation learning. It can be used to pre-train transformer networks using relatively little compute. ELECTRA models are trained to distinguish ""real"" input tokens vs ""fake"" input tokens generated by another neural network, similar to the discriminator of a [GAN](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.2661.pdf). At small scale, ELECTRA achieves strong results even when trained on a single GPU. At large scale, ELECTRA achieves state-of-the-art results on the [SQuAD 2.0](https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/) dataset.",apache-2.0,,,3,https://huggingface.co/google/electra-large-discriminator,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,23,,transformers,false
