tksluangrath/tool-concierge,5,mcp,downloads:desc,2026-07-31T16:17:05.000Z,2026-07-31T14:34:02.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,20,,"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) became a cross-vendor standard ""in a very short time span"" ([Anthropic, 2024](https://www.anthropic.com/news/model-context-protocol)). Models that hallucinate tool names or malform arguments turn these integrations into silent failures ([Patil et al., 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15334)). Routing every tool-use decision through a frontier model is also costly at scale, and small open-weight models fine-tuned on curated function-calling data can match or beat larger ones ([Erdogan et al., 2024](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.00608)). I fine-tuned [Qwen/Qwen3-8B-Base](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B-Base) with LoRA to generate a single MCP tool call, or an explicit `no_applicable_tool` abstention, from a plain-English request and a set of MCP tool defini",gpl-3.0,,,6,https://huggingface.co/tksluangrath/tool-concierge,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,0,,peft,false
