jakequist/kanjiland-annotation,4,from-scratch,downloads:desc,2026-07-17T01:24:02.000Z,2026-07-17T01:23:50.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,10,,"A from-scratch 52.3M Transformer that maps raw Japanese to the **full Kanjiland reading-comprehension format** — segmentation, furigana, glosses, word groupings, translation, and grammar labels (⟨T⟩/⟨W⟩/⟨S⟩/⟨G⟩), with **no MeCab at inference** (it learned segmentation itself). Part of [**Kanjiland**](https://github.com/jakequist/kanjiland).",mit,,,3,https://huggingface.co/jakequist/kanjiland-annotation,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,0,,,false
Probabilistr/slm-125m-raft-finetuned,4,from-scratch,downloads:desc,2026-07-24T05:13:06.000Z,2026-07-24T05:12:49.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,12,,"RAFT (Retrieval-Augmented Fine-Tuning) SFT of [Probabilistr/slm-125m-base](https://huggingface.co/Probabilistr/slm-125m-base) (a 125.8M-parameter from-scratch Llama-architecture model) -- unlike [Probabilistr/slm-125m-finetuned](https://huggingface.co/Probabilistr/slm-125m-finetuned) (single gold-passage SFT), this model is trained on 5 retrieved documents per example (80% include the oracle passage among distractors, the rest are all-distractor ""negative"" examples trained to answer ""Not stated in the context.""), so it learns to identify the right passage among retrieval noise and to refuse when none of the retrieved documents actually answer the question.",apache-2.0,,,3,https://huggingface.co/Probabilistr/slm-125m-raft-finetuned,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,0,,,false
