software-competence-center-hagenberg/PCFM,0,foundation-model,downloads:desc,2026-10-07T17:17:46.000Z,2026-08-26T00:58:00.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,15,,"PCFM is a **topology-constrained, any-variate time-series foundation model** for industrial process telemetry. Unlike existing time-series foundation models, it accepts a **directed, lag-annotated causal graph** `G(A, T)` — the physical topology of a plant — as an **inference-time structural prompt**: a GNN-style spatial router restricts cross-variate information flow to the graph's edges and reads each driver at its physical cause–effect lag, at a spatial cost linear in the edge count. Its learned parameters are independent of the number of input variates, so one set of pre-trained weights serves arbitrary sensor configurations.",apache-2.0,,,3,https://huggingface.co/software-competence-center-hagenberg/PCFM,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,2,,,false
JTF2000/ChorusTIC,0,foundation-model,downloads:desc,2026-09-29T11:01:06.000Z,2026-08-28T08:45:13.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,8,,ChorusTIC is a classification-native foundation model for training-free univariate and multivariate time series classification. It uses labeled context examples to predict query labels without fitting a target-specific classifier or updating model parameters.,mit,,,3,https://huggingface.co/JTF2000/ChorusTIC,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,1,,,false
SII-GAIR-NLP/RIBOSPAN-FM,0,foundation-model,downloads:desc,2026-09-01T17:49:10.000Z,2026-09-01T17:48:06.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,11,fill-mask,"Many full-length RNAs, particularly mRNAs, exceed the ~1K context lengths used to pretrain representative dense RNA encoders, forcing long transcripts to be truncated and preventing their 5′ UTR, CDS, and 3′ UTR from being modeled jointly at single-nucleotide resolution. **RiboSpan** is a **1.61B-parameter bidirectional Transformer** with **single-nucleotide tokenization**, **dense self-attention in every layer**, and **native long-context pretraining at up to 10,240 nt**. It is trained on **67.6 million RNA sequences comprising 85.7 billion nucleotides** from RNAcentral, Ensembl, and Ensembl Genomes.",other,ribospan-non-commercial-model-license,https://huggingface.co/SII-GAIR-NLP/RIBOSPAN-FM/blob/main/LICENSE,3,https://huggingface.co/SII-GAIR-NLP/RIBOSPAN-FM,noassertion,yes,LICENSE,LICENSE,full,file_only,"RIBOSPAN NON-COMMERCIAL MODEL LICENSE Version 1.0 Copyright © 2026 Shanghai Innovation Institute. All rights reserved except as expressly granted under this License. IMPORTANT NOTICE This RIBOSPAN Non-Commercial Model License (the ""License"") governs the use of RIBOSPAN Model Materials made available by Shanghai Innovation Institute (the ""Licensor""). By downloading, accessing where access is conditioned on acceptance, using, reproducing, modifying, fine-tuning, or distributing any RIBOSPAN Model Materials, you agree to be bound by this License. If you accept this License on behalf of an organization or other legal entity, you represent that you have authority to bind that entity to this License. If you do not agree to the terms of this License, you may not use the RIBOSPAN Model Materials. This License applies only to RIBOSPAN model weights, checkpoints, and other model-specific materials expressly released under this License. Source code separately released under the Apache License 2.0 is not governed by this License and remains subject to the Apache License 2.0. 1. DEFINITIONS 1.1 ""RIBOSPAN Model Materials"" ""RIBOSPAN Model Materials"" or ""Model Materials"" means RIBOSPAN model weights, pretrained checkpoints, model parameters, model-specific configuration files, weight indexes, tokenizer assets distributed as part of a model release, and other model-specific materials expressly distributed by the Licensor under this License. For clarity, source code separately released under the Apache License 2.0 is not included in the Model Materials. 1.2 ""Derivative Model"" ""Derivative Model"" means any model, checkpoint, or set of model parameters derived from, adapted from, or materially based on the RIBOSPAN Model Materials, including models produced through: (a) fine-tuning; (b) continued pretraining; (c) parameter-efficient fine-tuning; (d) adapters, LoRA, or similar parameter modifications; (e) model merging; (f) pruning; (g) quantization; (h) weight interpolation; (i) model c",license_other_raw/SII-GAIR-NLP/RIBOSPAN-FM/LICENSE,tag,2,,,false
