VITRA-VLA/VITRA-VLA-3B,0,pretraining,downloads:desc,2025-11-30T18:56:27.000Z,2025-11-30T15:51:05.000Z,2026-10-20 14:27:33,11,robotics,"VITRA is a novel approach for pretraining Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models for robotic manipulation using large-scale, unscripted, real-world videos of human hand activities. Treating human hand as dexterous robot end-effector, we show that in-the-wild egocentric human videos without any annotations can be transformed into data formats fully aligned with existing robotic V-L-A training data in terms of task granularity and labels. We create a human hand V-L-A dataset containing over 1 million episodes. We further develop a VLA model with a causal action transformer trained on this dataset. It demonstrates strong zero-shot human-hand action prediction in entirely new scenes and serves as a cornerstone for few-shot finetuning and adaptation to real-world robotic manipulation.",mit,,,3,https://huggingface.co/VITRA-VLA/VITRA-VLA-3B,yes,no,,,full,api_only,,,tag,4,,transformers,false
